{
  "title": "Other Aamal of The First Night",
  "data": "Sayyid Ibn Tawus reports that Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.) used to recite this supplication on the first night of Ramadan:\nاَللّٰهُمَّ رَبَّ شَهْرِ رَمَضَانَ مُنَزِّلَ الْقُرْاٰنِ هٰذَا شَهْرُ رَمَضَانَ الَّذِيْۤ اَنْزَلْتَ فِيْهِ الْقُرْاٰنَ\nALLAAHUMMA RABBA SHAHRI RAMADAANA MUNAZZILAL QUR'AANI HAADHA SHAHRU RAMADAANAL LAZEE ANZALTA FEEHIL QUR'AAN\nO Allah, Lord of the month of Ramadan, Revealer of the Qur'an! This is the month of Ramadan in which You revealed the Qur'an,\nوَ اَنْزَلْتَ فِيْهِ اٰيَاتٍ بَيِّنَاتٍ مِّنَ الْهُدٰى وَ الْفُرْقَانِ\nWA ANZALTA FEEHI AAYAATIM BAYYINAATIM MINAL HUDAA WAL FURQAAN\nand revealed therein clear proofs of the guidance and the Criterion.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ بَارِكْ لَنَا فِيْ شَهْرِ رَمَضَانَ وَ اَعِنَّا عَلٰى صِيَامِهٖ وَ صَلَاتِهٖ وَ تَقَبَّلْهُ مِنَّا\nALLAAHUMMA BAARIK LANAA FEE SHAHRI RAMADAANA WA A'INNAA A'LAA SIYAAMIHEE WA SALAATIH, WA TAQABBAL-HU MINNAA\nO Allah, bless us in the month of Ramadan, help us observe its fasting and prayers, and accept it from us.",
  "merits": "Devotional acts and supplications recommended on the first night of the holy month of Ramadan."
}
